{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-023",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 23,
  "title": "Job 23",
  "display_title": "Job 23",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 23,
  "sortOrder": 18023,
  "verseCount": 17,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Even to day is my complaint bitter: my stroke is heavier than my groaning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Oh that I knew where I might find him! that I might come even to his seat!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I would order my cause before him, and fill my mouth with arguments.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "I would know the words which he would answer me, and understand what he would say unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Will he plead against me with his great power? No; but he would put strength in me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "There the righteous might dispute with him; so should I be delivered for ever from my judge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Behold, I go forward, but he is not there; and backward, but I cannot perceive him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "On the left hand, where he doth work, but I cannot behold him: he hideth himself on the right hand, that I cannot see him:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But he knoweth the way that I take: when he hath tried me, I shall come forth as gold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "My foot hath held his steps, his way have I kept, and not declined.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Neither have I gone back from the commandment of his lips; I have esteemed the words of his mouth more than my necessary food.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But he is in one mind, and who can turn him? and what his soul desireth, even that he doeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For he performeth the thing that is appointed for me: and many such things are with him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Therefore am I troubled at his presence: when I consider, I am afraid of him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For God maketh my heart soft, and the Almighty troubleth me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:23:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Because I was not cut off before the darkness, neither hath he covered the darkness from my face.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 23:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:23:17"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
